        "timestamp": 1782048456,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Trump-backed de la Espriella or leftist Cepeda? Colombians elect a new president Americas Issued on: 21/06/2026 - 15:27 Colombians are heading to the polls this Sunday to elect a new president. The frontrunner is Abelardo de la Esperiella. He has vowed to return to full-scale military confrontation with armed groups. His challenger is leftwing senator Iván Cepeda, he argues for modifying the current peace plan, which seeks disarmament through negotiations. Six decades of conflict has killed hundreds of thousands of people, and each candidate has a starkly different vision on how to end it… Analysis by Mariano Aguirre Ernst, associate fellow at Chatam House's International Security Programme. Who is Ivan Cepeda, left-wing candidate in Colombia's presidential elections? 21/06/2026 Americas Bolivia deploys army to halt protests after declaration of state of emergency 21/06/2026 Americas Who is Abelardo de la Esperiella, far-right candidate in the Colombian presidential election? 21/06/2026 Americas Farewell, Scotland: Boston won’t forget the Tartan Army 20/06/2026 Sport Canadian beer prices test German fans' thirst at FIFA World Cup 20/06/2026 Americas Paint from Trump renovation peels off Washington's Reflecting Pool 20/06/2026 Americas Peru: Voters await result of presidential election, the closest in the country's history 20/06/2026 Americas Bolivia declares state of emergency, escalating a 50-day blockade crisis 20/06/2026 Americas Italy: Meloni says Trump 'made up' story that she 'begged' him for photo 19/06/2026 Europe"
