        "orario": "15:17",
        "timestamp": 1782047877,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Sailors trapped in Hormuz strait, dodging drones and rationing food Middle East Issued on: 21/06/2026 - 15:17 Despite the US-Iran talks which began today in Switzerland, the Strait of Hormuz is being kept shut today by the Iranians. Tehran accuses Israel of breaching the ceasefire agreement by continuing its strikes on Lebanon. The Strait’s closure has an array of impacts on the global economy… but also on the thousands of sailors, stranded on ships in the middle of an active conflict zone. To learn more about how they are dealing with the current situation, FRANCE 24 talked to Phil Belcher, the marine director at International Association of Independent Tanker Owners (Intertanko). Israel and Hezbollah trade fire, as US-Iran talks begin in Switzerland 21/06/2026 Middle East Iran claims Lebanon 'main topic' at peace talks with US 21/06/2026 Middle East US-Iran peace talks to begin, after Tehran closed Strait of Hormuz 21/06/2026 Middle East Iran closes Strait of Hormuz despite ceasefire after continued Israeli strikes in Lebanon 20/06/2026 Middle East Israel strikes Lebanon despite ceasefire, at least 16 killed 20/06/2026 Middle East NGOs in Lebanon denounce Israeli attacks on medics amid ceasefire 20/06/2026 Middle East Could Israel lose Donald Trump’s support by continuing to drop bombs in Lebanon? 20/06/2026 Middle East Hezbollah-Israel flare-up in Lebanon despite ceasefire announced by the USA 20/06/2026 Middle East US-Iran ceasefire negociations underway in Switzerland 20/06/2026 Middle East"
